**As a** developer using the library
**I want** to turn arbitrary text into a URL-safe slug
**So that** the scaffold's spec → test → verify loop is proven end to end

**Independent test:** `mise run -C {{.Dir}} test` proves the scenarios below
against the library.

# Acceptance Criteria

## Scenario 1: words become a lowercase, hyphenated slug

<!-- id: scenario.slug.create.basic -->

- Given the text "Hello World"
- When it is slugified
- Then the result is "hello-world"

## Scenario 2: punctuation collapses and hyphens are trimmed

<!-- id: scenario.slug.create.symbols -->

- Given the text "TypeScript & You!"
- When it is slugified
- Then the result is "typescript-you"
